    "---\n",
    "## 1. 🔄 List Comprehensions & Generator Expressions <a id='1'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "List comprehensions are a concise, Pythonic way to create lists from iterables. They are **30–50% faster** than equivalent `for` loops because they are optimized at the C level in CPython.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Generator expressions** look similar but use `()` instead of `[]`. The key difference:\n",
    "- **List comprehension** → evaluates *eagerly*, stores everything in memory at once.\n",
    "- **Generator expression** → evaluates *lazily*, yields one item at a time. Memory usage stays constant regardless of dataset size.\n",
    "\n",
    "### When to use which?\n",
    "| Situation | Use |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Need to iterate once over large data | Generator |\n",
    "| Need random access (index into results) | List |\n",
    "| Feeding into `sum()`, `max()`, `any()` | Generator |\n",
    "| Passing to a function that needs a list | List |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Engineering Context\n",
    "When processing millions of rows from a database or flat files, generators prevent `MemoryError` crashes. Always prefer generators in ETL pipelines when you only need to traverse data once."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept1-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Basic list comprehension ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Old-school loop\n",
    "evens_loop = []\n",
    "for x in range(20):\n",
    "    if x % 2 == 0:\n",
    "        evens_loop.append(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Comprehension equivalent — one clean line\n",
    "evens = [x for x in range(20) if x % 2 == 0]\n",
    "print(\"Evens:\", evens)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept1-code2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Nested comprehension for flattening data ──────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Imagine rows returned from a DB query as tuples\n",
    "db_rows = [(1, 'Alice', 'DE'), (2, 'Bob', 'SWE'), (3, 'Carol', 'DE')]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract only names of Data Engineers\n",
    "de_names = [name for _, name, role in db_rows if role == 'DE']\n",
    "print(\"Data Engineers:\", de_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Flatten a nested list (e.g., batched API responses)\n",
    "batched = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5], [6, 7, 8, 9]]\n",
    "flat = [item for batch in batched for item in batch]\n",
    "print(\"Flattened:\", flat)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept1-code3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Generator vs List — memory comparison ────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "N = 1_000_000\n",
    "\n",
    "list_result   = [x**2 for x in range(N)]       # Stores 1M integers in RAM\n",
    "gen_result    = (x**2 for x in range(N))        # Stores only the generator object\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"List size  : {sys.getsizeof(list_result):,} bytes\")\n",
    "print(f\"Generator  : {sys.getsizeof(gen_result):,} bytes\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nGenerators use essentially the same memory regardless of N!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept1-code4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Real DE use-case: streaming CSV rows through a generator ─────────────────\n",
    "import csv, io\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simulate a large CSV file in memory\n",
    "raw_csv = \"id,name,revenue\\n1,Alpha,5000\\n2,Beta,-200\\n3,Gamma,8000\\n4,Delta,-50\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def valid_records(file_obj):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Generator that yields only records with positive revenue.\"\"\"\n",
    "    reader = csv.DictReader(file_obj)\n",
    "    for row in reader:\n",
    "        if int(row['revenue']) > 0:\n",
    "            yield row   # <-- Only one row lives in memory at a time\n",
    "\n",
    "with io.StringIO(raw_csv) as f:\n",
    "    for record in valid_records(f):\n",
    "        print(record)"
   ]
