    "---\n",
    "## 2. 🧰 Itertools & Functools <a id='2'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "These two standard library modules implement powerful, memory-efficient tools for functional-style data manipulation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`itertools`** provides building blocks for working with iterables:\n",
    "- `chain` — merge multiple iterables without copying data\n",
    "- `groupby` — group consecutive elements (SQL `GROUP BY` equivalent)\n",
    "- `islice` — slice an iterator without materializing it\n",
    "- `product`, `combinations`, `permutations` — combinatorics\n",
    "- `batched` (Python 3.12+) — split data into fixed-size chunks\n",
    "\n",
    "**`functools`** provides higher-order function utilities:\n",
    "- `lru_cache` / `cache` — memoize expensive function calls\n",
    "- `reduce` — fold an iterable into a single value\n",
    "- `partial` — pre-fill function arguments to create specialized callables\n",
    "- `wraps` — preserve function metadata when writing decorators\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Engineering Context\n",
    "Itertools are indispensable when merging data from multiple sources, grouping records for aggregation, or chunking large datasets for batch inserts. `lru_cache` is a game-changer for caching repeated config lookups or schema fetches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept2-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import itertools\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── chain: Merge multiple data sources lazily ─────────────────────────────────\n",
    "jan_sales = [('P001', 100), ('P002', 200)]\n",
    "feb_sales = [('P001', 150), ('P003', 300)]\n",
    "mar_sales = [('P002', 250)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# No intermediate list created — all three are streamed together\n",
    "all_sales = itertools.chain(jan_sales, feb_sales, mar_sales)\n",
    "print(\"All sales:\")\n",
    "for product, amount in all_sales:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {product}: {amount}\")"
   ]
