    "---\n",
    "## 3. 📦 Context Managers (`with` statement) <a id='3'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "A context manager wraps a block of code with **setup** and **teardown** logic that runs automatically — even if an exception is raised inside the block.\n",
    "\n",
    "Under the hood, it uses the `__enter__` and `__exit__` dunder methods (or the `@contextmanager` decorator for a cleaner syntax).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why it matters for Data Engineers\n",
    "- **File handles** — forgetting to `.close()` causes data corruption or OS-level file descriptor leaks.\n",
    "- **Database connections** — unclosed connections exhaust connection pool limits, causing pipeline stalls.\n",
    "- **Locks & semaphores** — in concurrent pipelines, unreleased locks cause deadlocks.\n",
    "- **Temp files** — auto-cleanup of temp artifacts after processing.\n",
    "- **Transactions** — auto-commit or rollback DB transactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The `contextlib` Module\n",
    "`contextlib.contextmanager` lets you write a context manager as a simple generator, avoiding the boilerplate of a full class with `__enter__`/`__exit__`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept3-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Why context managers matter: resource leak example ────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "# ❌ Risky: if an exception occurs, file is never closed\n",
    "# f = open('data.csv')\n",
    "# data = f.read()   # <-- What if this throws?\n",
    "# f.close()         # <-- Never reached!\n",
    "\n",
    "# ✅ Safe: file always closed, even on exception\n",
    "import io\n",
    "data = \"col1,col2\\n1,a\\n2,b\"\n",
    "\n",
    "with io.StringIO(data) as f:\n",
    "    content = f.read()\n",
    "    print(\"Read:\", repr(content[:20]))\n",
    "# File is closed here — guaranteed\n",
    "print(\"File closed:\", f.closed)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept3-code2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from contextlib import contextmanager\n",
    "import time\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Custom context manager: pipeline timing ───────────────────────────────────\n",
    "@contextmanager\n",
    "def timer(task_name: str):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Measures and prints execution time of any code block.\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"[START] {task_name}\")\n",
    "    start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        yield  # <-- Code inside `with` block runs here\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
    "        print(f\"[END]   {task_name} — {elapsed:.4f}s\")\n",
    "\n",
    "with timer(\"Load and transform data\"):\n",
    "    # Simulated work\n",
    "    total = sum(x**2 for x in range(500_000))\n",
    "    print(f\"  Sum of squares: {total:,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept3-code3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Custom context manager: DB transaction simulation ────────────────────────\n",
    "@contextmanager\n",
    "def db_transaction(conn_string: str):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simulates a DB transaction that auto-commits or rolls back.\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"  Connecting to: {conn_string}\")\n",
    "    print(\"  BEGIN TRANSACTION\")\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        yield {\"conn\": conn_string, \"status\": \"open\"}  # yield the 'connection'\n",
    "        print(\"  COMMIT\")       # Only runs if no exception\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"  ROLLBACK (reason: {e})\")  # Runs if exception raised\n",
    "        raise\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        print(\"  Connection closed\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ✅ Successful transaction\n",
    "print(\"--- Successful transaction ---\")\n",
    "with db_transaction(\"postgresql://prod/db\") as conn:\n",
    "    print(f\"  Inserting records via {conn['conn']}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ❌ Failed transaction — auto rollback\n",
    "print(\"--- Failed transaction ---\")\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    with db_transaction(\"postgresql://prod/db\") as conn:\n",
    "        print(\"  Inserting records...\")\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"Duplicate primary key!\")\n",
    "except ValueError:\n",
    "    print(\"  Handled upstream.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept3-code4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Stacking context managers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import tempfile, os\n",
    "\n",
    "@contextmanager\n",
    "def temp_workspace():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Creates a temp directory and cleans it up automatically.\"\"\"\n",
    "    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmpdir:\n",
    "        print(f\"  Temp dir created: {tmpdir}\")\n",
    "        yield tmpdir\n",
    "    print(\"  Temp dir cleaned up!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stack two context managers\n",
    "with timer(\"ETL Job\"), temp_workspace() as workspace:\n",
    "    output_path = os.path.join(workspace, \"output.csv\")\n",
    "    with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n",
    "        f.write(\"id,value\\n1,100\\n\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Written to {output_path}\")"
   ]
