    "---\n",
    "## 4. 🏗️ Dataclasses & TypedDicts <a id='4'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "In data engineering, you constantly deal with structured data — pipeline configs, schema definitions, API responses, database records. Python offers several tools to model this cleanly:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Tool | Best for | Mutable | Validation | Default values |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `dict` | Simple, untyped data | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |\n",
    "| `TypedDict` | Dict-shaped data with type hints | ✅ | ❌ (static only) | ❌ |\n",
    "| `dataclass` | Structured objects with methods | ✅ | ❌ (static only) | ✅ |\n",
    "| `dataclass(frozen=True)` | Immutable config objects | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |\n",
    "| `pydantic.BaseModel` | Full runtime validation | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Dataclasses Beat Plain Dicts in Pipelines\n",
    "- **Autocomplete & static analysis** — IDEs know the fields and types\n",
    "- **`__repr__`** — automatic, readable string representation for logging\n",
    "- **`__eq__`** — automatic equality comparison\n",
    "- **Default values** — clean defaults without `dict.get()` everywhere\n",
    "- **Methods** — attach validation or transformation logic to the data itself"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept4-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from dataclasses import dataclass, field, asdict, astuple\n",
    "from typing import Optional\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Basic dataclass for pipeline config ───────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "@dataclass\n",
    "class IngestionConfig:\n",
    "    source_path: str\n",
    "    destination_table: str\n",
    "    batch_size: int = 1000\n",
    "    dry_run: bool = False\n",
    "    tags: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)  # Mutable default — must use field()\n",
    "    max_retries: int = 3\n",
    "    description: Optional[str] = None\n",
    "\n",
    "config = IngestionConfig(\n",
    "    source_path=\"s3://my-bucket/data/\",\n",
    "    destination_table=\"warehouse.sales\",\n",
    "    tags=[\"finance\", \"daily\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(config)               # __repr__ generated automatically\n",
    "print(\"Batch size:\", config.batch_size)\n",
    "print(\"As dict:\", asdict(config))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept4-code2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── frozen=True: Immutable config (hashable, safe to pass around) ─────────────\n",
    "@dataclass(frozen=True)\n",
    "class DBConnectionConfig:\n",
    "    host: str\n",
    "    port: int\n",
    "    database: str\n",
    "    user: str\n",
    "\n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def connection_string(self) -> str:\n",
    "        return f\"postgresql://{self.user}@{self.host}:{self.port}/{self.database}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "prod_db = DBConnectionConfig(host=\"prod-db.internal\", port=5432, database=\"warehouse\", user=\"etl_user\")\n",
    "print(prod_db.connection_string)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Frozen means immutable — this will raise a FrozenInstanceError:\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    prod_db.host = \"hacker.com\"  # type: ignore\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Cannot mutate frozen config: {type(e).__name__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
