    "---\n",
    "## 5. ⚡ Concurrency: Threading, Multiprocessing & AsyncIO <a id='5'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### The GIL — Python's concurrency constraint\n",
    "Python has a **Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)** that prevents multiple threads from running Python bytecode simultaneously. This shapes which concurrency tool to use:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Task Type | Example | Best Tool |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **I/O-bound** | API calls, DB queries, file reads | `asyncio` or `threading` |\n",
    "| **CPU-bound** | Data transformation, parsing, compression | `multiprocessing` |\n",
    "| **Mixed** | Read from API, transform, write to DB | `asyncio` + `ProcessPoolExecutor` |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decision Tree\n",
    "```\n",
    "Is work I/O-bound?  \n",
    "  └── Yes → Is it modern async-friendly code?  \n",
    "               └── Yes → asyncio  \n",
    "               └── No  → threading  \n",
    "  └── No (CPU-bound) → multiprocessing\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why it matters for Data Engineers\n",
    "Pipelines are almost always a mix: fetch from 10 APIs simultaneously (I/O), then crunch the numbers (CPU). Knowing how to parallelize each stage is the difference between a 2-hour job and a 10-minute job."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept5-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── asyncio: Concurrent I/O-bound tasks ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "import asyncio, time\n",
    "\n",
    "async def fetch_from_api(endpoint: str, delay: float) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simulates an async HTTP call.\"\"\"\n",
    "    await asyncio.sleep(delay)  # Non-blocking wait (simulates network I/O)\n",
    "    return {\"endpoint\": endpoint, \"rows\": 100}\n",
    "\n",
    "async def run_all_fetches():\n",
    "    endpoints = [\n",
    "        (\"https://api.sales.com/orders\",    1.2),\n",
    "        (\"https://api.crm.com/customers\",   0.8),\n",
    "        (\"https://api.finance.com/invoices\",1.5),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    # All 3 requests run concurrently — total time ≈ max(delays)\n",
    "    start = time.perf_counter()\n",
    "    results = await asyncio.gather(*[fetch_from_api(ep, d) for ep, d in endpoints])\n",
    "    elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
    "    print(f\"Fetched {len(results)} sources in {elapsed:.2f}s (sequential would be {sum(d for _,d in endpoints):.1f}s)\")\n",
    "    for r in results:\n",
    "        print(f\"  {r}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "await run_all_fetches()"
   ]
