    "---\n",
    "## 8. 🔍 Exception Handling & Custom Exceptions <a id='8'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "Robust exception handling is what separates a toy script from a production data pipeline. Unhandled exceptions in a pipeline can mean:\n",
    "- Silent data loss (partial writes with no error logged)\n",
    "- Corrupted state (half-written records)\n",
    "- No alerting (the job \"succeeded\" but did nothing)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exception Hierarchy Best Practices\n",
    "```\n",
    "PipelineError (base)\n",
    "├── DataValidationError\n",
    "│   ├── SchemaError\n",
    "│   └── NullConstraintError\n",
    "├── SourceConnectionError\n",
    "└── DestinationWriteError\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Having a custom exception hierarchy lets you:\n",
    "- Catch specific vs. broad errors at different layers\n",
    "- Attach structured metadata (field name, row number, value) to errors\n",
    "- Route errors to appropriate handlers (retry vs. alert vs. DLQ)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key clauses\n",
    "- `try` — code that might fail\n",
    "- `except SomeError as e` — handle specific exception\n",
    "- `else` — runs only if no exception was raised\n",
    "- `finally` — always runs (cleanup, close connections)\n",
    "- `raise ... from e` — chain exceptions, preserving context"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept8-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Custom exception hierarchy for a data pipeline ───────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "class PipelineError(Exception):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Base class for all pipeline errors.\"\"\"\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "class DataValidationError(PipelineError):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, field: str, value, message: str):\n",
    "        self.field = field\n",
    "        self.value = value\n",
    "        super().__init__(f\"Validation failed on '{field}' (value={value!r}): {message}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "class SchemaError(DataValidationError):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Missing required column or wrong type.\"\"\"\n",
    "    pass\n",
    "\n",
    "class SourceConnectionError(PipelineError):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, source: str, cause: Exception):\n",
    "        self.source = source\n",
    "        super().__init__(f\"Cannot connect to source '{source}': {cause}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test our exceptions\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    raise DataValidationError('age', -5, 'must be a positive integer')\n",
    "except PipelineError as e:   # Catches any subclass of PipelineError\n",
    "    print(f\"Caught PipelineError: {e}\")\n",
    "    if isinstance(e, DataValidationError):\n",
    "        print(f\"  Offending field: {e.field}, value: {e.value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept8-code2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Full try/except/else/finally pattern ─────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "def process_record(record: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    required = {'id', 'amount', 'currency'}\n",
    "    missing = required - record.keys()\n",
    "    if missing:\n",
    "        raise SchemaError('record', record, f\"Missing required fields: {missing}\")\n",
    "    if record['amount'] < 0:\n",
    "        raise DataValidationError('amount', record['amount'], 'must be non-negative')\n",
    "    return {**record, 'processed': True}\n",
    "\n",
    "test_records = [\n",
    "    {'id': 1, 'amount': 100.0, 'currency': 'USD'},  # Valid\n",
    "    {'id': 2, 'amount': -50.0, 'currency': 'EUR'},  # Invalid amount\n",
    "    {'id': 3, 'currency': 'GBP'},                   # Missing fields\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "successful = []\n",
    "failed = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for rec in test_records:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        result = process_record(rec)\n",
    "    except SchemaError as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"[SCHEMA ERROR] Record {rec.get('id', '?')}: {e}\")\n",
    "        failed.append(rec)\n",
    "    except DataValidationError as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"[VALIDATION ERROR] Record {rec.get('id', '?')}: {e}\")\n",
    "        failed.append(rec)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        successful.append(result)  # Only runs if no exception\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        pass  # Could close a per-record resource here\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSuccessful: {len(successful)}, Failed: {len(failed)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept8-code3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Exception chaining with `raise ... from` ──────────────────────────────────\n",
    "# Preserves the original traceback while adding pipeline-level context\n",
    "\n",
    "def connect_to_source(source_name: str):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        raise TimeoutError(\"Connection timed out after 30s\")  # Simulate low-level error\n",
    "    except TimeoutError as e:\n",
    "        # Wrap the low-level error in a domain-specific exception\n",
    "        raise SourceConnectionError(source_name, e) from e\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    connect_to_source(\"postgres://prod-db\")\n",
    "except PipelineError as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"Pipeline error: {e}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Original cause: {e.__cause__}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Source: {e.source}\")"
