    "---\n",
    "## 10. 📊 Profiling & Memory Optimization <a id='10'></a>\n",
    "\n",
    "### What & Why\n",
    "At scale, inefficient code has exponential costs. A function that wastes 100ms and 10MB of memory is unnoticeable on 100 rows — but catastrophic on 100 million rows.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Profiling** helps you find where time and memory are actually being spent (the bottleneck is almost never where you expect).\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tools Overview\n",
    "| Tool | Purpose | Use when |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `time.perf_counter()` | Manual timing | Quick checks |\n",
    "| `timeit` | Accurate micro-benchmarks | Comparing implementations |\n",
    "| `cProfile` | Function-level CPU profiling | Finding slow functions |\n",
    "| `memory_profiler` | Line-by-line memory usage | Tracking memory leaks |\n",
    "| `tracemalloc` | Built-in memory tracing | Production-safe profiling |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Memory Optimization Techniques\n",
    "- **Generators** over lists where possible\n",
    "- **`__slots__`** for memory-efficient classes\n",
    "- **Chunked reading** with Pandas\n",
    "- **Appropriate dtypes** in Pandas (e.g., `int8` instead of `int64`)\n",
    "- **Delete** large objects with `del` when no longer needed\n",
    "- **Parquet** over CSV for storage efficiency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept10-code1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import timeit, cProfile, pstats, io\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── timeit: Compare two implementations ──────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "def approach_loop(n):\n",
    "    result = []\n",
    "    for x in range(n):\n",
    "        if x % 2 == 0:\n",
    "            result.append(x ** 2)\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "def approach_comprehension(n):\n",
    "    return [x**2 for x in range(n) if x % 2 == 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "N = 10_000\n",
    "reps = 500\n",
    "\n",
    "t_loop = timeit.timeit(lambda: approach_loop(N), number=reps)\n",
    "t_comp = timeit.timeit(lambda: approach_comprehension(N), number=reps)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loop          : {t_loop:.4f}s total ({t_loop/reps*1000:.3f}ms each)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Comprehension : {t_comp:.4f}s total ({t_comp/reps*1000:.3f}ms each)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Speedup       : {t_loop/t_comp:.2f}x faster\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "concept10-code2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── cProfile: Find the real bottleneck in a pipeline ─────────────────────────\n",
    "import cProfile, pstats\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract(): return list(range(100_000))\n",
    "def transform(data): return [x * 2 for x in data if x % 3 == 0]\n",
    "def load(data): return sum(data)  # Simulated write\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_pipeline():\n",
    "    raw = extract()\n",
    "    transformed = transform(raw)\n",
    "    result = load(transformed)\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "# Profile into a string buffer\n",
    "profiler = cProfile.Profile()\n",
    "profiler.enable()\n",
    "run_pipeline()\n",
    "profiler.disable()\n",
    "\n",
    "stream = io.StringIO()\n",
    "stats = pstats.Stats(profiler, stream=stream).sort_stats('cumulative')\n",
    "stats.print_stats(10)  # Top 10 functions by cumulative time\n",
    "print(stream.getvalue())"
   ]
  },
